  "answer": "The study confirmed one of the five challenging cases it was looking for, so the goal was not met. Scene 023b7fcc with cars 0.5 s earlier and at 2x speed made the policy collide in every repeat, and its range sits above one half (S1). The policy is to blame and none of the failures look like simulator artifacts. In those runs the ego follows lead car 66 too closely and hits it instead of braking. It then steers left into the next lane and hits car 61. That is a following-and-swerve failure, and it's not clear a cut-in caused it. No other setting on the other eight scenes failed even once. Settings repeated three times stayed below one half. Settings run only once or twice are a hint, not a rate, so the study can't say whether the other scenes have a challenging case.",
